From: HybridGt <hybridgt@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:22:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Queues: honour queue fence waits
 (VICTORY_QUEUE_WAITS=1) (HybridGt)

Queue::Wait did nothing and every ExecuteCommandLists ran at once, so
work the title ordered behind another queue's signal ran before it and
read data never written. A queue with an unmet wait now holds its later
executions, signals and waits in order; each fence signal runs what it
unblocks; a wait unmet after 4 s runs anyway (logged).

RTX 4070 Ti, run17: world from frame 1790 to 2449+ with no device removal
(runs 3-16: removed 0-300 frames into the world), no wait hit the limit.
Picture still black.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
